invariant: INV-16
file: src/rsa_sign64_blind.h
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: blinded_prime_exponent reads r as zero, so each half walks dp
  and dq themselves, the same exponent every signature. Every signature
  is still the same bytes, so no signature test notices.
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test reads the blinded exponents and holds each to
  d + r (p - 1) computed a byte at a time.

--- old
        r = (r << 8) | r_bytes[i];
--- new
        r = (r << 8) & r_bytes[i];
